dding:12px 14px}.slc-wrap .slc-table tbody tr:last-child{border-bottom:0}.slc-wrap .slc-table tbody th{width:auto;padding:0 0 8px;border:0;font-weight:600;color:var(--slc-fg)}.slc-wrap .slc-table tbody td{width:auto;padding:8px 10px;border:0;border-radius:6px}.slc-wrap .slc-table tbody td+td{margin-top:6px;background:var(--slc-muted)}.slc-wrap .slc-table tbody td::before{content:attr(data-slc-label);display:block;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--slc-mfg);margin-bottom:2px}.slc-wrap .slc-pre{font-size:.74rem;padding:14px}}\n.slc-wrap .slc-btns{flex:none;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px}\n.slc-wrap .slc-btn-2{background:transparent;color:var(--slc-accent-text)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-btn-2:hover{background:var(--slc-card);color:var(--slc-accent-text)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-note{margin:10px 0 0;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--slc-mfg)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-note a,.slc-wrap .slc-table a,.slc-wrap .slc-code-note a{color:var(--slc-accent-text)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-also a{color:var(--slc-accent-text);text-decoration:none}\n.slc-wrap .slc-also a:hover{text-decoration:underline}\n.slc-wrap .slc-table sup,.slc-wrap .slc-note sup{font-size:.7em;line-height:0}\n\n.slc-wrap .slc-eyebrow-note{margin-top:14px;font-size:.92rem;color:var(--slc-mfg)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-panel-hero{margin-top:34px}\n.slc-wrap .slc-bullets{margin:0;padding-left:20px;color:var(--slc-mfg)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-bullets li{margin:0 0 10px}\n.slc-wrap .slc-bullets strong{color:var(--slc-fg)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-stay,.slc-wrap .slc-switch{margin-top:36px}\n.slc-wrap .slc-stay{padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--slc-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--slc-card)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-move-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px;margin:18px 0 4px}\n.slc-wrap .slc-move-grid>div{padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--slc-border);border-radius:12px;background:var(--slc-card)}\n.slc-wrap .slc-move-title{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:1rem}\n.slc-wrap .slc-move-grid code{font-size:.86em}\n.slc-wrap .slc-also{margin-top:22px;font-size:.95rem;color:var(--slc-mfg)}\n@container (max-width:640px){.slc-wrap .slc-move-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px}.slc-wrap .slc-stay{padding:18px}}\n</style>\n<div class=\"slc-head\"><p class=\"slc-kicker\">SendLit vs beehiiv</p><h1 class=\"slc-h2\">beehiiv prices by subscribers. SendLit prices by emails sent.</h1><p class=\"slc-lead\">At 10,000 subscribers sending weekly, beehiiv Lite is $139/month. SendLit Pro is $29 plus about $4–$6 of Amazon SES for those 40,000 emails. Contacts are unlimited on every SendLit plan, so growing your list never moves you to a higher tier by itself.</p><div class=\"slc-eyebrow-note\">Compared at real list sizes below, including what beehiiv still does better.</div></div>\n<section class=\"slc-panel slc-panel-hero\" id=\"slc-panel-beehiiv\"><h2 class=\"slc-h3\">Side by side</h2><p class=\"slc-intro\">beehiiv is a hosted newsletter platform with a website builder, growth tools and monetization built in. It prices by subscriber, so the bill climbs with your list. Hosted SendLit prices by the emails you send, with unlimited contacts, and everything in the app is in the REST API, with an MCP server for everything you do day to day.</p><div class=\"slc-table-card\"><div class=\"slc-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Hosted SendLit and beehiiv comparison table\"><table class=\"slc-table\"><caption class=\"slc-sr\">Hosted SendLit compared with beehiiv</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Feature</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"slc-col-sl\">SendLit (hosted)</th><th scope=\"col\">beehiiv</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Monthly cost at 10k subscribers, weekly<sup>1</sup></th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><strong>About $33–$35/mo</strong>: Pro $29 + about $4–$6 of Amazon SES for 40,000 emails</td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\">Lite: $139/mo billed monthly ($119/mo billed yearly)</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Monthly cost at 100k subscribers, weekly<sup>1</sup></th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><strong>About $139–$163/mo</strong>: Business $99 + about $40–$64 of Amazon SES for 400,000 emails</td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\">Lite: $469/mo billed monthly ($399/mo billed yearly)</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Pricing model</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>Per email sent, never per contact. Unlimited contacts on every plan: Free, then $10, $29 or $99/mo. Your provider bills delivery at its own rates</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-n\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4.5 4.5l7 7M11.5 4.5l-7 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">No: </span>Per subscriber: Lite from $49/mo billed yearly ($59 monthly) for 1,000 subscribers</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Sending and reputation</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>Your own Amazon SES, SMTP, Postmark, Resend, SendGrid or Mailgun account, so your sender reputation stays yours. Automatic warm-up included</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-p\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 8h8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Partly: </span>beehiiv’s own sending; dedicated IPs on Enterprise</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">REST API for every app action, plus MCP</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>Yes. Everything in the app is in the <a href=\"https://docs.sendlit.app/api-reference/\">REST API</a>, and the <a href=\"https://docs.sendlit.app/developers/mcp/\">MCP server</a> lets your AI agents do everything you do day to day</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-p\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 8h8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Partly: </span>Partly. REST API on every plan, but creating posts needs Pro or Enterprise, automations are read-only in the API, and MCP write access starts on Lite</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Servers to run</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>None. Sign up at app.sendlit.app and connect your sending account; we run and upgrade the servers</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>None, it’s hosted</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Free plan</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>Free forever: 3,000 emails a month, unlimited contacts</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>Free up to 2,500 subscribers</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Multi-step sequences</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>On every plan, including Free. Start on signup, or when a tag is added or removed</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>Automations, on Lite and above</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Transactional email API</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>On every plan: <code>emails.send</code> in the SDK or the REST API</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-p\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 8h8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Partly: </span>Send API, on Pro only</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Teams for your customers</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>3 teams on Pro, 15 on Business, plus a provisioning API to create one per customer</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-p\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 8h8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Partly: </span>3 publications on Lite, 10 on Pro; not an email team per customer with its own API key</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">API and SDKs</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>Typed TypeScript SDK (<a href=\"https://docs.sendlit.app/developers/sdk/\"><code>npm i sendlit</code></a>) with retries</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>REST API and an official TypeScript SDK</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">No lock-in</th><td data-slc-label=\"SendLit (hosted)\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">Yes: </span>Open source (<a href=\"https://github.com/codelitdev/sendlit\">AGPL-3.0 on GitHub</a>): self-host the same code anytime</span></span></td><td data-slc-label=\"beehiiv\"><span class=\"slc-cell\"><svg class=\"slc-ic slc-ic-n\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4.5 4.5l7 7M11.5 4.5l-7 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"slc-sr\">No: </span>Closed source, hosted only</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class=\"slc-note\"><sup>1</sup> Weekly means 4 emails per subscriber a month: 40,000 emails at 10k subscribers and 400,000 at 100k. SendLit Pro ($29/mo) includes 125,000 emails and Business ($99/mo) 600,000 (<a href=\"https://sendlit.app/pricing\">sendlit.app/pricing</a>). <a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/ses/pricing/\">Amazon SES</a> bills $0.10 per 1,000 emails à la carte or $0.16 on its Essentials plan. beehiiv: <a href=\"https://www.beehiiv.com/pricing\">beehiiv.com/pricing</a> slider at 10,000 and 100,000 subscribers, and its <a href=\"https://developers.beehiiv.com/api-reference/posts/create\">API reference</a>. All prices billed monthly in USD, checked 6 November 2026.</p><h4 class=\"slc-h4\">Add a subscriber to hosted SendLit</h4><div class=\"slc-codes\"><figure class=\"slc-code\"><figcaption class=\"slc-code-head\"><span>TypeScript SDK</span><span class=\"slc-chip\">Node.js</span></figcaption><pre class=\"slc-pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code>import { SendLit } from &quot;sendlit&quot;;\n\nconst sendlit = new SendLit({ apiKey: process.env.SENDLIT_API_KEY });\nawait sendlit.contacts.create({\n  email: &quot;ada@example.com&quot;,\n  name: &quot;Ada Lovelace&quot;,\n});</code></pre><p class=\"slc-code-note\">The SDK calls <code>https://api.sendlit.app</code> by default. A new contact starts every active sequence that triggers on signup; repeat signups return the existing contact and don’t re-enroll it.</p></figure><figure class=\"slc-code\"><figcaption class=\"slc-code-head\"><span>REST API</span><span class=\"slc-chip\">curl</span></figcaption><pre class=\"slc-pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code>curl https://api.sendlit.app/contacts \\\n  -H &quot;x-sendlit-apikey: $SENDLIT_API_KEY&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;content-type: application/json&quot; \\\n  -d &#x27;{&quot;email&quot;:&quot;ada@example.com&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ada Lovelace&quot;}&#x27;</code></pre><p class=\"slc-code-note\">Every action in the app has an endpoint in the <a href=\"https://docs.sendlit.app/api-reference/\">API reference</a>. Prefer an agent? Connect it to <code>https://api.sendlit.app/mcp</code> (<a href=\"https://docs.sendlit.app/developers/mcp/\">MCP docs</a>).</p></figure></div><h4 class=\"slc-h4\">Questions</h4><div class=\"slc-faq\"><details class=\"slc-faq-item\"><summary>Why does the cost gap grow with my list?</summary><p>beehiiv prices by subscriber count: Lite is $139 a month at 10,000 subscribers and $469 at 100,000, billed monthly. Hosted SendLit prices by emails sent, with unlimited contacts, so 100,000 subscribers emailed weekly is Business at $99 plus about $40–$64 of Amazon SES.</p></details><details class=\"slc-faq-item\"><summary>What do I need to get started?</summary><p>A free SendLit account and a sending account you connect, such as Amazon SES, Postmark or any SMTP server. If you use Amazon SES, AWS reviews your account before it lets you send to everyone.</p></details><details class=\"slc-faq-item\"><summary>Can I import my beehiiv list?</summary><p>Yes. Import beehiiv’s CSV export into SendLit; the subscription tier becomes a tag.</p></details><details class=\"slc-faq-item\"><summary>Does SendLit build a newsletter website?</summary><p>No. SendLit sends email. beehiiv also hosts your newsletter’s website and monetization tools.</p></details></div><section class=\"slc-panel slc-stay\" id=\"stick-with-beehiiv\"><h2 class=\"slc-h3\">Stick with beehiiv if…</h2><p class=\"slc-intro\">We'd rather you pick the right tool than migrate twice. beehiiv wins in some clear cases:</p><ul class=\"slc-bullets\"><li><strong>Your newsletter makes money from sponsors or paid subscriptions.</strong> beehiiv has the Ad Network, paid tiers and a sponsorship storefront built in. SendLit doesn't take payments, and paid subscribers would have to re-subscribe if you left.</li><li><strong>You want a website, not an archive.</strong> beehiiv has a full site builder with custom domains, custom pages, redirects and site analytics. SendLit's web archive is a reader-facing archive of your sends.</li><li><strong>You're under 2,500 subscribers and happy on Free.</strong> beehiiv Free has unlimited sends at that size, which SendLit's Free plan (3,000 emails a month) doesn't match.</li><li><strong>You don't want to own deliverability.</strong> SendLit sends through your SES or SMTP account. You choose the provider, request SES production access if you need it, and your reputation is yours to manage.</li><li><strong>You run a podcast or community alongside the newsletter.</strong> Beehiiv has both. SendLit is email only.</li></ul></section><section class=\"slc-panel slc-switch\" id=\"switch-to-sendlit\"><h2 class=\"slc-h3\">What moves with you, and what stays</h2><p class=\"slc-intro\">Export from beehiiv, import the CSV as it is, and keep your sending domain so inbox providers see the same sender.</p><div class=\"slc-move-grid\"><div><h3 class=\"slc-move-title\">Moves with you</h3><ul class=\"slc-bullets\"><li>Every subscriber and their status</li><li>Tiers, as tags like <code>tier:premium</code></li><li>Custom fields and signup dates</li><li>Open and click history as contact fields</li><li>Your sending domain and its reputation</li><li>Signup forms (hosted or embedded) and welcome emails as sequences</li></ul></div><div><h3 class=\"slc-move-title\">Stays on beehiiv</h3><ul class=\"slc-bullets\"><li>Past posts and the archive (export them; import isn't built yet)</li><li>Paid subscriptions</li><li>Referral program, recommendations and boosts</li><li>Ad network, podcast and community</li></ul></div></div><p class=\"slc-note\">Plan on a short overlap: send your first SendLit issue while beehiiv is still live, then swap the signup embeds and turn beehiiv off. <a href=\"https://docs.sendlit.app/migrate/beehiiv\">Read the step-by-step migration guide</a>.</p></section><div class=\"slc-cta\"><div><p class=\"slc-cta-title\">Start on hosted SendLit</p><p class=\"slc-cta-text\">Free forever for 3,000 emails a month, then $10, $29 or $99. Unlimited contacts on every plan, and nothing to run.</p></div><div class=\"slc-btns\"><a class=\"slc-btn\" href=\"https://app.sendlit.app\">Start free</a><a class=\"slc-btn slc-btn-2\" href=\"https://sendlit.app/pricing\">See pricing</a></div></div></section>\n<p class=\"slc-also\">Also comparing? <a href=\"/compare\">All SendLit comparisons</a> · <a href=\"/pricing\">SendLit pricing</a></p>\n<p class=\"slc-foot\"><sup>1</sup> Weekly means 4 emails per subscriber a month: 10,000 subscribers = 40,000 emails (SendLit Pro); 100,000 = 400,000 emails (Business). Prices checked 6 November 2026: <a href=\"https://www.beehiiv.com/pricing\">beehiiv pricing</a> (Lite monthly $139 at 10k, $469 at 100k; Pro $239/$699) and <a href=\"https://sendlit.app/pricing\">SendLit pricing</a>. SES at $0.10–$0.16 per 1,000 emails makes 40k about $4–$6 and 400k about $40–$64. SendLit plan prices exclude your provider's delivery charges. Features compared from each product's public docs. Spotted something out of date? <a href=\"https://github.com/codelitdev/sendlit/issues\">Open an issue</a>.</p>\n</div>"
      }
    }
  ]
}
